#: ../../../autoapi/tilelang/cuda/language/gemm_op/index.rst:149
msgid ""
"This is the explicit asynchronous Hopper WGMMA counterpart to the default "
"synchronous `T.gemm(...)` interface, with two stricter guarantees: - it "
"always requests the WGMMA lowering path - it never auto-emits an inlined "
"`warpgroup_wait`"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../autoapi/tilelang/cuda/language/gemm_op/index.rst:154
msgid ""
"If the current target or operand pattern cannot use Hopper WGMMA, "
"compilation fails instead of silently falling back to MMA."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../autoapi/tilelang/cuda/language/gemm_op/index.rst:162
msgid ""
"This is the explicit asynchronous Blackwell TCGEN5MMA counterpart to the "
"default synchronous `T.gemm(...)` interface, with two stricter guarantees: - "
"it always requests the TCGEN5MMA lowering path - it never auto-emits an "
"inlined `mbarrier_wait_parity`"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../autoapi/tilelang/cuda/language/gemm_op/index.rst:167
msgid ""
"``mbar=None`` omits the completion arrival for an intermediate issue.  A "
"later TCGEN05 operation remains ordered in the same issue stream and may "
"publish the completion event for the whole sequence."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../autoapi/tilelang/cuda/language/gemm_op/index.rst:171
msgid ""
"When ``use_2cta=True``, the instruction is lowered to the 2CTA variant which "
"requires ``cluster_dims`` to be ``(2,1,1)`` or ``(1,2,1)``."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../autoapi/tilelang/cuda/language/gemm_op/index.rst:174
msgid ""
"If the current target or operand pattern cannot use Blackwell TCGEN5MMA, "
"compilation fails instead of silently falling back to another GEMM path."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../autoapi/tilelang/cuda/language/gemm_op/index.rst:182
msgid ""
"This is the explicit counterpart of `T.gemm_blockscaled(...)` for Blackwell "
"TCGEN5MMA, with the same guarantees as `T.tcgen05_gemm(...)`: it always "
"requests the TCGEN5MMA lowering path and compilation fails instead of "
"silently falling back if that path is unavailable. It never auto-emits an "
"inlined `mbarrier_wait_parity`."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../autoapi/tilelang/cuda/language/gemm_op/index.rst:188
msgid ""
"``mbar=None`` omits the completion arrival for this issue. The caller must "
"publish completion with a later TCGEN05 operation or an explicit ``T."
"tcgen05_mma_arrive`` before waiting and consuming the result."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../autoapi/tilelang/cuda/language/gemm_op/index.rst:192
msgid ""
"With ``use_2cta=True``, this lowers to the true 2CTA block-scaled TCGEN05 "
"path only; there is no fallback or emulation. That mode requires "
"``cluster_dims`` to be ``(2,1,1)`` or ``(1,2,1)``."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../autoapi/tilelang/cuda/language/gemm_op/index.rst:196
msgid ""
"A and B are FP8/FP6/FP4 mxf8f6f4 operands in shared memory, C is the "
"accumulator in tensor memory, and SFA/SFB are E8M0 scale factors already "
"resident in tensor memory. The API is explicit-async: it issues the MMA and "
"leaves synchronization to the user schedule."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../autoapi/tilelang/cuda/language/gemm_op/index.rst:201
msgid ""
"``k_start`` is the logical K-axis start offset for this MMA tile. "
"``sf_a_granularity_k`` and ``sf_b_granularity_k`` describe how many K "
"elements one packed scale factor covers. The compiler derives the PTX scale-"
"factor A/B IDs for each internal K32 MMA atom from these values."
msgstr ""

